        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Neck pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Midline and paraspinal neck pain extending into the right shoulder, rated 4–7/10; worse at the end of the workday, while sitting at a computer, and while driving. Sleep is broken by neck pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Intermittent subjective limb heaviness, shakiness, and clumsiness"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports a vague feeling of heaviness, shakiness, or clumsiness in the right arm more than the left, and sometimes the right leg. Episodes last minutes to 1 hour and occur several times daily. She remains able to type and lift light things, but says the limbs feel off. Onset timing is uncertain and the account has varied: possibly the week before the visit or immediately after the crash."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Intermittent tingling"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent tingling in the right forearm and hand, not clearly dermatomal."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
